361: \subsection{Second-order moment map}\label{disp_map}
362: The second-order \hi\ moment map extracted from the NA \hi\ data cube is shown in Fig.~\ref{mom2}.  The highest second-order moments are found near the stellar core of the galaxy.  The radial profile of the second-order moment map is shown in Fig.~\ref{disp_prof}.  If the second-order moments are interpreted as a measure of the gas velocity dispersion, then the average outer disk dispersion of $\sigma_{gas}\sim$ 10 km s$^{-1}$ is close to the constant gas velocity dispersion value of  $\sigma_{gas}=11$~\kms\ found by \citet{leroy_THINGS} for a sample of THINGS dwarf galaxies.
